    {
      "id": "p0174-b006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Because the Japanese script translates \"determination\" as ketsui, this line's wordplay would be lost in a straightforward translation. To get around this obstacle, the translator replaced \"you're filled with detemmienation\" with the Japanese Temminese equivalent of \"you're filled with determination\". The resulting Japanese line no longer relies on wordplay, but it does remain humorous and Temmie-themed.",
        "raw": "Because the Japanese script translates \"determination\" as ketsui, this line's\nwordplay would be lost in a straightforward translation. To get around this\nobstacle, the translator replaced \"you're filled with detemmienation\" with\nthe Japanese Temminese equivalent of \"you're filled with determination\".\nThe resulting Japanese line no longer relies on wordplay, but it does remain\nhumorous and Temmie-themed.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29495195,
          0.37117143,
          0.87958941,
          0.475
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28691959,
          0.37045714,
          0.91515838,
          0.47607143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          46,
          47,
          48,
          49,
          50,
          51
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "日文把 determination 译作 ketsui（决心），因此直接翻译就会失去文字游戏。为解决这个问题，译者把“你充满了 detemmienation”换成了用日语 Temmie 语写的“你充满了决心”。新版不再依赖双关，却仍然好笑，也仍然与 Temmie 有关。",
        "status": "draft",
